            <ArticleTitle>Toxic effects of epidural analgesia with ropivacaine 0.2% in a diabetic patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 51-year-old ASA physical status II, non-insulin-dependent diabetic male patient manifested lower limb nerve injury after receiving postoperative epidural analgesia with ropivacaine 0.2%. The case is presented, including a discussion of the relation between local anesthetic toxicity and diabetic neuropathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
